WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.077
If you're a fulfillment by Amazon, FBA Seller, the Inventory Defect and Reimbursement IDR Portal

00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:15.000
can help streamline how you manage inventory-related defects, damages, and losses.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.830
The Portal consolidates inventory health data from multiple reports into a single dashboard, making

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:27.740
it easier to track inventory problems and gather information needed to file reimbursement claims.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:35.292
Additionally, it  automatically applies FBA reimbursement policy checks, saving you the time of

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:36.386
manually researching

00:00:36.386 --> 00:00:37.480
reimbursable opportunities.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.913
To access the IDR Portal in Seller Central, open the main menu, hover

00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:46.540
over Inventory, and select FBA Inventory.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.590
From the FBA Inventory Dashboard, click the Inventory

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:54.420
drop-down, and select Inventory Defect and Reimbursement.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.451
The IDR Overview page displays

00:00:56.451 --> 00:01:03.357
a summary of your total affected units and their defect status, featuring a trend chart that can

00:01:03.357 --> 00:01:05.388
help you track defect patterns

00:01:05.388 --> 00:01:06.200
over time.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.800
These trends can help you investigate common issues that may need to be addressed for improvement.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:19.469
For example, if you notice a high number of warehouse damage defects for a particular SKU, you might

00:01:19.469 --> 00:01:21.533
want to evaluate your product

00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:25.660
packaging, or consider additional protective materials to reduce future damages.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:29.674
Defects in the IDR Portal are organized

00:01:29.674 --> 00:01:34.580
into three main tabs, eligible for claim, in progress, and resolved.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:39.279
You can customize your views using filters to focus on a

00:01:39.279 --> 00:01:46.734
specific date range, search for products by SKU, asin, or FNSKU, and sort by defects that occurred

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:47.553
within the

00:01:47.553 --> 00:01:50.420
warehouse or during the customer return process.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:56.442
Each tab also contains a bar chart that visually organizes defect types by

00:01:56.442 --> 00:02:00.000
volume, helping you identify your most frequent issues.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.114
You can also select from a drop-down menu to filter and view affected

00:02:05.114 --> 00:02:06.940
units within specific defect types.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:13.084
On the eligible for claim tab, you'll find a list of Inventory Defects that qualify for

00:02:13.084 --> 00:02:13.420
reimbursement.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.360
The In Progress tab displays defects currently under Amazon's Review.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.850
The Resolved tab provides a

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:26.648
comprehensive view of defects that have been addressed, detailing the reasoning behind Amazon's

00:02:26.648 --> 00:02:27.540
resolution decision.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:35.540
The Resolution Distribution Pie Chart categorizes outcomes as reimbursed, reconciled, or ineligible.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.265
If you disagree

00:02:37.265 --> 00:02:43.693
with a resolution, you can submit a case with seller support, including the Product Defect Information

00:02:43.693 --> 00:02:44.497
and a

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.300
Detailed Explanation.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:51.911
We encourage you to leverage the IDR Portal regularly to refine your inventory management

00:02:51.911 --> 00:02:52.320
strategies.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:59.738
For more information, visit the Inventory Defect and Reimbursement IDR Portal Help page in Seller

00:02:59.738 --> 00:03:00.180
Central.
